WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.318
Mindwtr brings the Getting Things Done
workflow to your phone.

00:00:04.643 --> 00:00:09.252
It is free and open source, works offline,
and needs no account.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.887
Today's Focus is your deliberate
shortlist. Star an action for today.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.803
Fold the other groups to see only your
chosen actions.

00:00:21.407 --> 00:00:24.008
Starring does not change the task's
schedule;

00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:27.595
other dated work stays under Today.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.278
Capture a thought before it escapes.

00:00:31.487 --> 00:00:35.144
Add useful context while you type, then
keep moving.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.126
A home screen widget puts the same quick
capture one tap away.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.637
Clarify with the guided Inbox processor,
one decision at a time.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.851
Decide whether it is actionable, define
the next action,

00:01:00.886 --> 00:01:04.520
and organize it by project, area, or
context.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.522
Or use Quick mode when you want every
choice on one screen.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.944
File the last item, and Inbox Zero
restores trust without

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:20.033
turning cleanup into a score.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.109
Now engage. Focus groups Today, Review
Due, and Next Actions.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.324
Show details when useful, then hide them
for calm.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:39.069
Filter by priority, energy, time, project,

00:01:39.104 --> 00:01:42.366
or context, and watch the list update.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.247
Swipe either way to reveal quick actions
before choosing one.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.116
Long press and drag to reorder today's
Focus list around real priorities.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.408
Simple by default means a clean list
instead of a cockpit.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.218
Open an action to reveal priority,
project, context,

00:02:07.241 --> 00:02:09.226
and the details you need.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.844
Open any action to adjust its schedule.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.401
Open Menu to reach the rest of your
system.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.497
Choose Projects.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.811
Then open Website Redesign.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.644
Projects keep multi-step outcomes visible.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.490
Choose Sequential or Parallel, then decide
whether sequential

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.159
order runs across sections or within each
section.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.061
Within a project, sectioned tasks stay
readable,

00:02:52.095 --> 00:02:56.112
and reorder mode lets the plan evolve
without rebuilding it.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.937
Board filters narrow the picture before
you move anything.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.487
Drag Draft agenda from Inbox to Next, and
both column counts update.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:21.441
Then scroll through Next, Waiting, and
Someday to see the whole status flow.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.770
Calendar turns scheduled work into a plan
you can see.

00:03:29.211 --> 00:03:32.009
Day keeps timed commitments precise.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.137
Week widens the view without losing the
time of day.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.168
Keep swiping across the Week view to move

00:03:51.203 --> 00:03:54.744
from one day to the next and reveal the
rest of the week.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:01.019
Slide the day control to compare a tighter
window with more of the week.

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.643
Reflect with a guided Weekly Review.

00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:11.472
Check the next seven days for commitments
and unfinished preparation.

00:04:14.917 --> 00:04:17.378
Check contexts for next actions.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:20.381
Review active projects for a real next
action,

00:04:20.462 --> 00:04:23.133
then finish with a system you can trust.

00:04:23.967 --> 00:04:28.843
Finish with a manageable next step, never
a streak, score, or guilt trip.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:34.739
Optional Mind Sweep uses gentle prompts to
uncover loose ends.

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:37.947
Capture whatever each prompt surfaces,

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.604
moving from home and belongings to work
and admin.

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:49.261
Finish with those thoughts safely
collected for later clarification.

00:04:50.867 --> 00:04:56.254
Mindwtr offers multiple themes, so your
workspace feels calm and personal.

00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:58.646
Nord feels calm and cool.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:06.043
Switch once more, and Sepia brings a
warmer tone.

00:05:06.417 --> 00:05:10.353
Optional AI is off by default and uses a
bring your own key,

00:05:10.469 --> 00:05:13.290
or BYOK, model.

00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:20.350
Open General settings to customize Quick
Access.

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:24.654
Choose Review, Projects, Calendar, or
Contexts.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:29.039
Projects moves into the bottom bar, while
Review remains in Menu.

00:05:29.517 --> 00:05:33.093
One tap now opens Projects and the project
page.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.993
Mindwtr is free and open source.

00:05:37.272 --> 00:05:41.533
Send feedback in the app without an
account, or create a GitHub issue.

00:05:42.717 --> 00:05:47.036
Capture, clarify, organize, reflect, and
engage across your devices.
